package com.lyra.blocker

data class FeatureLesson(val title: String, val artwork: String, val explanation: String, val access: String,
    val destination: AdminPage? = null, val personalTab: String = "Focus")

/** A guide explains a real control; illustrations never replace labels, consent or actual state. */
val featureLessons = listOf(
    FeatureLesson("Your phone. Your attention.", "attention-garden", "Start small: choose one thing you want time for. M57 can hold a few distractions while you do it. You choose which boundaries fit your day.", "The timer needs no account. App protection needs Android accessibility."),
    FeatureLesson("Who holds the controls?", "personal-controls", "Personal use lets you change your own settings. Family use keeps protection changes behind an administrator password. Everyone can still use the personal focus timer.", "Existing family installations keep their administrator and password.", AdminPage.OVERVIEW),
    FeatureLesson("Bring Lyra along, if you like.", "learning-detour", "Supported AI apps and screens can take a detour into Lyra's learning space. Switch AI redirection off to use M57 independently. Other controls have their own switches.", "No Lyra account is required for M57. The optional handoff contains only a source-family hint and a new-chat request.", AdminPage.AI),
    FeatureLesson("One thing at a time.", "one-thing", "Name your intention and choose a timer. Apps and sites on your focus list wait until your focus phase ends. Other apps stay available.", "Choose the list in Plan. Accessibility must be connected to hold apps and supported browser addresses."),
    FeatureLesson("Breaks belong in the plan.", "take-a-breath", "Pomodoro alternates focus rounds and scheduled breaks. Your personal focus list rests during each break. A family rule, daily limit or overlapping routine can still apply.", "A personal break never pauses administrator protection or the family DNS filter."),
    FeatureLesson("Make the next scroll a choice.", "short-video-choice", "Choose a blocking screen or a gentle dismissible reminder on supported short-video viewers. Ordinary videos and chats use different screens and should stay available.", "Needs accessibility. App updates, languages and hidden controls can affect recognition.", AdminPage.SHORT_VIDEOS),
    FeatureLesson("Enough for today.", "daily-allowance", "Give a chosen app a daily time allowance. When the local estimate reaches it, M57 holds that app until the next local day. You can edit or remove your own limits.", "Needs optional Usage Access and connected accessibility. Android estimates and split-screen timing can differ.", AdminPage.APP_LIMITS),
    FeatureLesson("Let a routine remember.", "routine-rhythm", "Pick days and a start/end time. Your focus list repeats at those times, including across midnight. A routine has its own schedule, separate from a timer break.", "Follows this phone's timezone. Enforcement needs connected accessibility and may be delayed if Android suspends the service.", AdminPage.ROUTINES),
    FeatureLesson("Choose your browsing boundaries.", "browsing-boundaries", "Use a personal focus-site list, a study-site allowlist, or optional family website categories. A study exception cannot override an administrator's family rule.", "Browser rules need a visible supported address. The local DNS VPN is a filter; it does not encrypt general traffic.", AdminPage.FAMILY),
    FeatureLesson("A permission with a purpose.", "permission-window", "Accessibility recognises app identities and supported screen controls so M57 can show its boundary screen. Read the explanation before granting access. You can review or revoke Android access later.", "M57 does not read message bodies or save browsing history. Usage access, VPN and device administrator are separate optional permissions.", AdminPage.DEVICE_ACCESS),
    FeatureLesson("A little perspective.", "local-history", "Look back at your saved focus sessions and optional app-time estimates. A day with less focus is simply a day, not a failed streak. Keep what helps; delete what does not.", "Up to 500 session records stay in private app storage. App-use events are processed locally and are not retained.", personalTab = "Insights"),
    FeatureLesson("Your data, here.", "privacy-drawer", "Your settings and focus history stay on this phone. Export only when you choose a document destination. Deleting history clears saved session records; exported files remain yours to manage.", "Android backups are disabled. Family-list downloads and optional Lyra navigation are separate network actions.", personalTab = "Settings"),
    FeatureLesson("Choose a commitment you can keep.", "commitment-ribbon", "A commitment timer or Pomodoro has no early-end button. Personal protection settings and focus-boundary changes wait until it ends. Choose a realistic duration before you start.", "Android controls and calling remain available. This is a personal commitment, not tamperproof device management."),
    FeatureLesson("A small direction for today.", "small-goal", "Choose the number of focus minutes that feels useful. The daily goal is a direction you can change, without a streak, leaderboard or penalty.", "Sessions count toward the local day they end. The goal does not grant authority over family settings.", personalTab = "Plan"),
    FeatureLesson("Make room for your day.", "ready-for-your-day", "You can use the timer now. Add app, video or website controls when you want them, then check Home for connection health. Every feature is included.", "No ads, premium switches or account requirement. Source and license notices are in Settings.", personalTab = "Home"),
    FeatureLesson("A first page, whenever you like.", "first-page", "Your first saved session begins the history. You can finish a normal session early, return another day, or clear the page and start again.", "A running session is separate from saved history. Deleting history does not stop its timer.", personalTab = "Insights")
)
